From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] OpenSSL 1.0.1u for Android 4.2: openssl.config,
 openssl.version, the Android patches and the 4.3 build files

The recipe for the next commit (import_openssl.sh output); together they move
external/openssl from 1.0.1c (android-4.2.2_r1) to upstream 1.0.1u.

openssl.config and patches/ are those of the 4.3 series (patches/jb/4.3)
without channelid.patch, kktls_channelid_key.patch and
kktls_channelid_state.patch: stock 4.2 has no Channel ID, and its fields sit
in the middle of struct ssl_st. tls12_digests.patch: SSL3_STATE hunk context
without the Channel ID fields. Android.mk, Apps.mk, Crypto.mk, Ssl.mk,
android-config.mk, import_openssl.sh and check-all-builds.sh from
android-4.3_r3 (generated *-config.mk instead of hand-kept source lists); in Crypto.mk and
Ssl.mk the ARM target libraries build with LOCAL_SDK_VERSION 9 as in stock
4.2, so libcrypto links and exports the libgcc helpers (__aeabi_*,
_Unwind_*) that stock prebuilt binaries import from it.
patches/README starts with a note on this base (patches of the 4.2 set not
carried and why).

kktls_jb_cipher_auth_decl.patch (this base only): the ssl.h prototype of
SSL_CIPHER_authentication_method, which the 4.4 base gets from
channelid.patch.
