+
+Fixes the Clang based build.
+
+tls12_digests.patch
+
+Fixes a bug with handling TLS 1.2 and digest functions for DSA and ECDSA
+keys.
+
+alpn.patch
+
+This change adds support for ALPN in OpenSSL. ALPN is the IETF
+blessed version of NPN and we'll be supporting both ALPN and NPN for
+some time yet.
+
+rc4_md5_harden.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2017-3731 (fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2k, after the last 1.0.1 release):
+a truncated record of the stitched RC4-MD5 cipher made the payload length wrap
+around. LineageOS cm-11.0 carried the same fix (be01785) for its 1.0.1e tree.
+
+cve-2022-0778.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2022-0778 (fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2zd/1.1.1n, after the last 1.0.1
+release): BN_mod_sqrt() did not finish for some non-prime p, reachable from
+explicit EC parameters in a peer certificate. Upstream 3118eb6493, unchanged.
+
+cve-2023-2650.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2023-2650 (fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2zh/1.1.1u, after the last 1.0.1
+release): OBJ_obj2txt() took O(n^2) time for a gigantic OID sub-identifier;
+OIDs longer than 586 bytes are now rejected. Upstream 9e209944b3, unchanged
+(CHANGES/NEWS hunks dropped).
+
+cve-2026-35189.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2026-35189 (fixed upstream in 2026, after the last 1.0.1 release):
+each nameRelativeToCRLIssuer CRL distribution point of a parsed certificate
+cost a copy of the issuer name; the name is now built only during CRL
+matching. Hand port of upstream c72ae182ca: a static helper in x509_vfy.c
+instead of the new internal ossl_dist_point_name_full(), no new exported
+symbol.
+
+cve-2018-0739.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2018-0739 (fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2o, after the last 1.0.1 release):
+recursive ASN.1 types (PKCS7) could overflow the stack with deeply nested
+input; d2i now stops at a constructed nesting depth of 30. Upstream
+9310d45087, unchanged.
+
+cve-2018-0732.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2018-0732 (fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2p, after the last 1.0.1 release):
+DH key generation now rejects primes above OPENSSL_DH_MAX_MODULUS_BITS, so a
+DHE server cannot make the client hang. Upstream 3984ef0b72, unchanged.
+
+cve-2024-5535.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2024-5535 (fixed upstream in 2024, after the last 1.0.1 release):
+SSL_select_next_proto() read past an empty client protocol list. Hand port
+of upstream cf6f91f612 with explicit bounds checks instead of the PACKET
+API; return values and the match result are unchanged, an empty or
+malformed client list now gives *out = NULL, *outlen = 0.
+
+cve-2020-1971.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2020-1971 (fixed upstream on the 1.1.1 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): GENERAL_NAME_cmp() compared an EdiPartyName through ASN1_TYPE_cmp()
+over a struct that is not an ASN1_TYPE, a NULL deref reachable from a crafted
+GENERAL_NAME. Adapted from upstream f960d81215: adds edipartyname_cmp() and
+splits GEN_X400/GEN_EDIPARTY in set0_value/get0_value. x400Address stays
+ASN1_TYPE* here; the GEN_X400 half is fixed by cve-2023-0286.patch.
+
+cve-2021-4160.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2021-4160 (fixed upstream on the 1.1.1 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): a dropped carry in the doubled cross term of bn_sqr_comba8/4 gave a
+wrong square for some inputs on 32-bit MIPS. Adapted from upstream e9e726506c
+(crypto/bn/asm/mips.pl; bn-mips.S is regenerated by the import). The upstream
+bntest.c regression vectors are copied verbatim into test_mod_exp_mont5 and
+run by the upstream `make test` (pruned from the Android import).
+
+cve-2021-23841.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2021-23841 (fixed upstream on the 1.1.1 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): X509_issuer_and_serial_hash() ran strlen() on a NULL
+X509_NAME_oneline() result for a malformed issuer. Adapted from upstream
+122a19ab48: adds a NULL check. OpenSSL itself does not call the function.
+
+cve-2023-0286.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2023-0286 (fixed upstream on the 1.1.1 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): GENERAL_NAME_cmp() compared x400Address (parsed as an ASN1_STRING)
+with ASN1_TYPE_cmp(), a type confusion / read primitive. Adapted from
+upstream 2c6c9d439b: compares with ASN1_STRING_cmp(); the union field keeps
+its ASN1_TYPE* declaration (no ABI change), so the compare casts. 1.0.1u has
+no v3nametest.c, so a minimal self-contained port of the upstream 97ab3c4b53
+GENERAL_NAME_cmp test carries the {0xa3,0x00} regression entry and is wired
+into test/Makefile; both are run by the upstream `make test` only.
+
+cve-2026-45447.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2026-45447 (fixed upstream in 2026, after the last 1.0.1 release):
+PKCS7_verify() freed the caller-owned indata on the error path
+(BIO_free_all), a use-after-free / double-free. Adapted from upstream
+9dfd688ad2: pops and frees only the BIOs in front of indata.
+
+cve-2026-22796.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2026-22796 (fixed upstream in 2026, after the last 1.0.1 release):
+PKCS12 parse_bag() and PKCS7_digest_from_attributes() read an ASN1_TYPE value
+union without checking its tag. Adapted from upstream 572844beca: validates
+the tag (friendlyName BMPSTRING, localKeyID / messageDigest OCTET_STRING)
+before use. The upstream apps/s_client.c hunk does not apply to 1.0.1u.
+
+Tier 2 backports B: cheap conditional fixes that an earlier triage marked
+"skip" because no in-tree caller reaches them; backported anyway as defensive
+depth since each is small and ABI-neutral.
+
+cve-2017-3735.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2017-3735 (fixed upstream on the 1.0.2 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): v3_addr_get_afi() read data[0]/data[1] of an addressFamily shorter
+than 2 bytes. Upstream 31c8b26559, unchanged. v3_addr.c is not compiled under
+the recipe (no-rfc3779); source-only hardening for any build that enables it.
+
+cve-2018-0737.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2018-0737 (fixed upstream on the 1.1.0 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): RSA key generation leaked the primes through a cache timing side
+channel. Adapted from upstream 6939eab03a: sets BN_FLG_CONSTTIME on rsa->p and
+rsa->q in the generator. (1.0.1u lacks the earlier r2 CONSTTIME hardening; that
+is a separate non-CVE item, out of scope here.)
+
+cve-2019-1559.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2019-1559 (fixed upstream on the 1.0.2 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): a 0-byte-record padding oracle survived because the connection was
+not put in the error state after a fatal alert. Adapted from upstream
+e9bbefbf0f: ssl3_read_bytes/dtls1_read_bytes and ssl3_send_alert set
+s->state = SSL_ST_ERR (which already exists in 1.0.1u).
+
+cve-2019-1563.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2019-1563 (fixed upstream on the 1.0.2 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): PKCS7/CMS decryption was a Bleichenbacher padding oracle. Upstream
+e21f8cf78a, pkcs7 hunks only (crypto/cms is not built): pkcs7_decrypt_rinfo()
+takes a fixlen argument and a zero-length or wrong-length decrypted key forces
+the existing MMA random-key fallback so padding validity no longer leaks.
+
+cve-2023-0215.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2023-0215 (fixed upstream on the 1.1.1 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): BIO_new_NDEF() left the caller's BIO chained to a freed asn_bio on
+the error path (use-after-free). Adapted from upstream c3829dd882: detaches the
+caller BIO with (void)BIO_pop(pop_bio) before BIO_free on error. 1.0.1u's
+asn1_bio_free() does not free ex_arg, so SET_EX_ARG is kept and ndef_aux is
+still freed on error (no leak, no double free).
+
+cve-2023-0465.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2023-0465 (fixed upstream on the 1.1.1 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): an invalid certificate policy on a leaf was silently ignored.
+Adapted from upstream b013765abf: check_policy()'s bad-extension loop starts at
+i=0 so the leaf is reported to the verify callback, with an internal-error
+guard. Ported to 1.0.1u's int-return convention; existing error macros.
+
+cve-2023-3446.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2023-3446 (fixed upstream on the 1.1.1 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): DH_check() ran BN_is_prime_ex() on an uncapped modulus (DoS). Upstream
+8780a89654: caps BN_num_bits(dh->p) at OPENSSL_DH_CHECK_MAX_MODULUS_BITS
+(32768) and returns DH_R_MODULUS_TOO_LARGE. The limit macro and the
+DH_F_DH_CHECK function code are plain ABI-neutral #defines (DH_R_MODULUS_TOO_
+LARGE already existed in 1.0.1u).
+
+cve-2024-0727.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2024-0727 (fixed upstream on the 3.0 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): a malformed PKCS#12 with an absent ContentInfo content caused NULL
+derefs. Adapted from upstream 09df4395b5: NULL checks in PKCS12_unpack_p7data /
+_p7encdata / _authsafes (p12_add.c), pkcs12_gen_mac (p12_mutl.c), newpass_p12
+(p12_npas.c) and SMIME_write_PKCS7 (pk7_mime.c). Uses existing PKCS12err codes;
+p7encdata returns NULL silently (no function code in 1.0.1u). No new macros.
+
+cve-2025-69421.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2025-69421 (fixed upstream on the 3.0 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): PKCS12_item_decrypt_d2i() dereferenced a NULL ASN1_OCTET_STRING.
+Adapted from upstream 36ecb49608 (the 1.0.1u name has no _ex suffix): rejects a
+NULL oct with the existing PKCS12_F_PKCS12_ITEM_DECRYPT_D2I / DECODE_ERROR.
+
+cve-2026-28388.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2026-28388 (fixed upstream on the 3.0 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): check_delta_base() dereferenced a delta CRL with no crlNumber.
+Upstream 59c3b31585, unchanged: returns 0 before ASN1_INTEGER_cmp when
+delta->crl_number is NULL. Reachable only under X509_V_FLAG_USE_DELTAS.
+
+cve-2017-3737.patch
+
+kktls: CVE-2017-3737 (fixed upstream on the 1.0.2 branch, after the last 1.0.1
+release): after a fatal error in the handshake, SSL_read()/SSL_write() called
+directly passed data unprotected, because SSL_in_init() was false in the
+error state. Upstream 898fb884b7, unchanged: SSL_ST_ERR = (0x05|SSL_ST_INIT).
+This also makes the cve-2019-1559 error state effective. Macro value only;
+SSL_cutthrough_complete() matches only its two read states, so stays false.
+
+cve-2024-5535-npn.patch
+
+kktls: follow-up of CVE-2024-5535 (upstream 3.0 159921152f): the client fails
+the handshake with handshake_failure when the NPN select callback returns OK
+with selected_len == 0 (before, OPENSSL_malloc(0) returning NULL made it an
+internal_error). A non-OK return keeps the 1.0.1u internal_error alert.
+
+kktls_channelid_key.patch
+
+kktls: SSL(_CTX)_set1_tls_channel_id accepts only an EC key on P-256 (KitKat
+checked EVP_PKEY_bits() == 256 only); ssl3_get_channel_id() checks the
+BN_new() results; SSL_CTRL_GET_CHANNEL_ID rejects a negative length.
+
+kktls_channelid_state.patch
+
+kktls: the KitKat channelid patch copied the SSL_CTX Channel ID settings in
+ssl3_new(), which runs again on a method change (SSL_clear,
+SSL_set_ssl_method, SSL_copy_session_id, SSL_dup): the key reference leaked
+and per-SSL settings were reset. Copied once in SSL_new() now. The
+tlsext_channel_id_valid flag is cleared at the start of each ClientHello and
+ServerHello extension parse, so a renegotiation does not inherit it.
+
+kktls_cert_chain.patch
+
+kktls: CERT_PKEY.cert_chain (KitKat jsse patch, owned after
+SSL_use_certificate_chain) is freed in ssl_cert_free() and duplicated with
+new references in ssl_cert_dup() (was leaked, and lost on a CERT copy).
+
+kktls_jb_cipher_auth_decl.patch
+
+kktls (Android 4.1/4.2 base): ssl.h declares SSL_CIPHER_authentication_method,
+which the jsse patch defines in ssl_ciph.c and calls from
+SSL_authentication_method() in ssl_lib.c. In the 4.4 base the prototype comes
+with channelid.patch, which this base does not carry; stock 4.1/4.2 had the
+same implicit declaration (a const char * returned as int).
+
+kktls_p12_npas_alg_get.patch
+
+kktls: PKCS12_newpass() alg_get() dereferenced the PBE parameter without
+checking that it is present and a SEQUENCE (1.1.0+ uses
+ASN1_TYPE_unpack_sequence(), which checks; 1.0.1u lacks it).
+
+kktls_alpn_empty.patch
+
+kktls: the server ALPN path rejects a select callback that returns OK with
+selected_len == 0 (internal_error, as before through OPENSSL_malloc(0)
+returning NULL; now explicit). Companion of cve-2024-5535-npn.
 
-This patch eliminates memory stores to addresses below SP.
+cve-2016-8610.patch
 
+ssl3_read_bytes() and dtls1_read_bytes() count consecutive warning alerts
+and fail with SSL_R_TOO_MANY_WARN_ALERTS (409) at 5; a non-empty non-alert
+record resets the count. Counter in the private CERT, as upstream 1.0.2
+(shared between two SSLs after SSL_copy_session_id, as there; 1.1.0 moved it
+per-SSL).
 
-mips_private.patch:
